Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 14:41:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] gateway: a byte cap after the stream has begun says
 request_too_large, so pi compacts

What changed
- A 413 that arrives after the stream's headers are already out is an error event. Pi reads that text alone and compacts on request_too_large, which writeErrorSaid already put on the JSON body. The event now says the same word, and Chat and Anthropic name that type. Gemini keeps its own status shape. It is not turned into context_length_exceeded.

Run
- At a15e576, TestStreamedByteCapSaysRequestTooLargeToPi failed: HTTP 200, a keepalive, then an error event whose type was api_error and whose text was "A: 413 Request Entity Too Large".
- With the fix, that test plus TestPayloadTooLargeSaysRequestTooLargeToPi, TestStreamErrorSaysItPasses, TestGroupLastFailureInStreamSaysItPasses, TestQuietCodexStreamKeptAliveThroughReplyWriters and TestMiddlewareOnAndOff passed in 8.6s.
- gofmt of the four Go files was clean. go vet -tags nogui and CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -tags nogui for windows, linux and darwin exited 0.
- go test -tags nogui -count=1 -p 2 -timeout 45m ./internal/gateway/ ran 2703s then failed: the known TestClaudeAsRootEnv and TestSweepBridgeProjectsTakesOnlyTheBridgesFolders, plus TestQuietCodexStreamKeptAliveThroughReplyWriters and TestMiddlewareOnAndOff while middleware logged "took too long" (both passed alone afterwards), and the 45m timeout. This is not a green package run.

